  "report_period": "Week 4 (17th Jan to 24th Jan 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "OceanPal have committed their Capesize \"Salt Lake City\" 171/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 16,2 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Star Triumph\" 176/2004 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold back in September at USD 20 mill. The Panamax \"Fame\" 75/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) of Target Marine was committed at USD 8,6 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Argolis\" 76/2005 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold recently at USD 8,2 mill. On the Supramax sector, Polforce Shipping committed their \"Papayiannis III\" 58/2010 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) at mid-high USD 11 mill. Remind you that back in September, the one-year-younger \"Kibali\" 57/2011 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 08/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 16,7 mill. Furthermore, Sotirakou S committed their \"Protector St. Raphael\" 56/2010 Xiamen, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 11 mill, while the one- year-younger \"Jag Rishi\" 56/2011 Cosco, China (SS/DD 03/2026, BWTS fitted) of Great Eastern Shipping was committed to Chinese interests at high USD 11 mill. In addition, Tolani Group committed their \"Prabhu Mihikaa\" 55/2005 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) to Vietnamese interests at low USD 10 mill. Note that a month ago, the \"SSI Nemesis\" 56/2005 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 10,9 mill. Precious Shipping have committed the Handysize \"Rojarek Naree\" 29/2005 Shikoku, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 09/2027, BWTS fitted) at USD 8,5 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"Ken Toku\" 29/2005 Shikoku, Japan (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in October at the same price. Moreover, Zodiac Maritime committed their \"Woodgate\" 28/2011 I-S, Japan (SS/DD 05/2026, BWTS fitted) to Vietnamese interests at USD 10,5 mill, while the one-year-younger \"POS Oceania\" 28/2012 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in October at USD 10,9 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Aframaxes \"Amax Anthem\" 116/2011 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 09/2026, BWTS fitted) & \"Amax Avenue\" 115/2010 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) were committed to undisclosed interests at USD 39,5 mill each. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the 2012-built sister vessel \"Nissos Delos\" 115/2012 Samsung, Korea (SS 08/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 45,3 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 6,000/7,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 4,000/6,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 4,000/6,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 3,000/4,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. West African trips via US Gulf into Continent were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 13,000 pd for 5/7 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 14,100 pd basis delivery China for 1 year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 6,000/8,000 pd. South East Asian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 2,000/5,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 4,000/6,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 10,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 60K/100K. South African trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 6,000/7,000 pd. West African trips into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. US Gulf trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from Japan into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. South East Asian trips into Australia were reported at the level of usd 3,000/5,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were fixed around usd 6,000 pd. West African trips were reported at the level of usd 4,000/5,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
